      "problem": "Compute $\\text{E}[-3X-2]$ if $\\text{E}[X]=-2.$",
      "worked_solution": "For any constants $a$ and $b$ and any random variable $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX+b]=a\\text{E}[X]+b.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[-3X-2] & =-3\\text{E}[X]-2 \\\\  & =-3(-2)-2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
